          "filename": "Salalah to Somerset 1982 - Syria (1706200716).jpg",
          "caption": "The Citadel is a large medieval fortified palace in the centre of the old city of Aleppo. The use of the hill can be traced to the middle of the 3rd millennium BC, as referenced in Cuneiform texts from Ebla and Mari. The prophet Abraham is said to have milked his sheep on the citadel hill which was damaged by the Mongol invasion of 1260 and again destroyed by the second Mongol invasion led by Tamerlaine which swept through Aleppo in 1400-1.   In 1415 the Mamluk governor of Aleppo, prince Sayf al-Din Jakam, rebuilt the citadel, which by then stood at the centre of a significant trading city of between 50-100,000 inhabitants.",
